error_signature: "ImportError: Error relocating .*: PyMem_Free: symbol not found"
root_cause: "CPython extension modules built on this device do not record libpython in DT_NEEDED, and the interpreter binary is not linked with -export-dynamic so its CPython symbols are not in the global scope; the dynamic loader therefore cannot resolve the CPython API symbols used by the extension."
rec_approach: "Run the test with the interpreter's shared library preloaded: LD_PRELOAD=<prefix>/lib/libpython3.12.so. Only needed while the extension's DT_NEEDED lacks libpython3.12.so.1.0 — extensions that do link it (e.g. PyQt6-sip) load fine without the preload. Check with `llvm-readelf -d` before adding it."
match_keywords: ["Error relocating", "symbol not found", "PyMem_Free", "LD_PRELOAD", "libpython3.12.so", "DT_NEEDED"]
severity:               2
category: platform
